# The simpler, the better in Russian: чем проще, тем лучше
subtitle: "Чем проще, тем лучше; вдвое дешевле; не столько цена, сколько вкус: comparing in Russian as Tom and Sofia set the menu and prices of «Кухонька»."
tags: ["russian","чем тем","russian comparatives","menu in russian","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/comparatives","vocabulary/kitchen"]
thumb: "band \"The simpler, the better\" stamp \"ЧЕМ … ТЕМ\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Russian style registers: spoken, scientific, official","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/209-russian-three-registers.cast"}

## The simpler, the better in Russian: чем проще, тем лучше
